# Block-Krylov calibration v1 mechanical failure

The first calibration task exited before any dense matrix operation. `scipy.io.mmread`
returned a COO matrix, while the script attempted direct row slicing. The preserved
traceback is in the task receipt stderr and reports `TypeError: 'coo_matrix' object is
not subscriptable` at `sparse[:512]`.

The repair is limited to converting the Matrix Market object to CSR before slicing.
The preregistered data, seeds, depths, metrics, thresholds, and comparisons are
unchanged. The replacement has a new script, output, and task identifier; the failed
task and original script remain intact.
